body:
The hook object validation doesn't handle the case where `hook.object` is an array of strings. According to the HookSchema definition, the `object` field can be either a string or an array of strings (`z.union([z.string(), z.array(z.string())])`). The current code only checks if the string value exists in the object names set, but doesn't iterate over array elements when `hook.object` is an array. This will cause false negatives where valid hook definitions with multiple objects won't be validated properly.
```suggestion
      if (!hook.object) {
        continue;
      }

      const hookObjects = Array.isArray(hook.object) ? hook.object : [hook.object];

      for (const objectName of hookObjects) {
        if (!objectNames.has(objectName)) {
          errors.push(
            `Hook '${hook.name}' references object '${objectName}' which is not defined in objects.`,
          );
        }
      }
```
